From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:13:25 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ws-carts

WonderSwan carts get their own wide shell in the retro bitmap renderer,
a 66 by 41 mm cart with the oval nameplate on top and the connector
step below, in two plastics: solid black for a WonderSwan game and
frosted clear (translucent, the board showing through) for a
WonderSwan Color game. The footer's colour flag picks the shell, and
the extension (.wsc clear, .ws black) when the footer cannot be read; a
colour set in Config/cart_shell.txt still wins. The shell outline and
nameplate are our own drawing; the two plastic colours and the 66 by
41 mm size are nelynes/slotPlus's
(https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/77fd357,
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/21cc4b0, GPL-3.0). The
retro_neutrals example pins the disc's grain seed, so adding shells
keeps every existing neutral byte for byte.
